{"archetypes":[{"name":"quiet-contract-capture","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The delegation from ci-status.sh to ci-behind-count.sh captures output via $() which only captures FD 1 (stdout), but emit_kv in lib-quiet.sh routes to FD 3 in quiet mode; if production mode routes BEHIND_COUNT only to FD 3, _behind_out is always empty and BEHIND_COUNT defaults to 0, silently breaking the CI-behind guard.","prompt_body":"Examine scripts/ci-status.sh lines 620-626 in the diff: `_behind_out=$(\"$SCRIPT_DIR/ci-behind-count.sh\" ... 2>/dev/null || echo \"\")` captures only stdout (FD 1). In scripts/ci-behind-count.sh, output is emitted via `emit_kv BEHIND_COUNT` which uses the lib-quiet.sh contract (FD 3). Determine whether `larch_quiet_init` in lib-quiet.sh routes `emit_kv` to stdout (FD 1) or to FD 3 in production mode (when LARCH_QUIET_DISABLE is NOT set). If emit_kv only reaches FD 3, then _behind_out is empty in production, BEHIND_COUNT defaults to 0 via the case guard, and the branch is never detected as behind — a silent correctness regression. Cross-check with how test-ci-status.sh invokes the delegation and whether LARCH_QUIET_DISABLE is set. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"ci-fix-state-lifecycle","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"CI_FIX_REBASE_PENDING is a module-level flag set inside _stage_and_push_ci_fixes and cleared only on successful push; it can persist stale into subsequent calls or across phase transitions (ci-initial → ci-merge), causing unintended git-force-push.sh on later calls that did not perform a rebase.","prompt_body":"Review scripts/ship-pr.sh focusing on the CI_FIX_REBASE_PENDING flag (declared at module level ~line 1109). Trace every code path in _stage_and_push_ci_fixes where the flag is set to true (failed git-add, git-commit, verify_rc=4, and the default case) and where it is cleared (only on successful push). Determine whether the flag can persist across (a) early-return paths before the rebase block, (b) successive calls within the same phase when the first call failed before reaching the push, and (c) transitions from ci-initial to ci-merge via run_ci_phase. Verify that the plan's stated intent ('CI_FIX_REBASE_PENDING is set only on a failed post-rebase verify path') matches the actual code paths. Check whether a stale true value in a subsequent call that does NOT rebase (behind=0) would incorrectly force-push a tree that was never rebased in that invocation. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"rebase-arg-parse","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"run_rebase_rebump's new positional argument parser uses a case-*) arm that silently consumes up to two positional args as base_remote and base_ref after the optional 'defer-push' keyword; mismatched call sites or future callers passing args in a different order could silently set the wrong base, causing rebase to target the wrong remote.","prompt_body":"Examine the new argument parser added to run_rebase_rebump in scripts/ship-pr.sh (the while-loop after `shift`). The case `*)` arm assigns `base_remote=$1; shift; [ \"$#\" -gt 0 ] || break; base_ref=$1; shift` — this means any unknown token is silently treated as base_remote. Audit every call site of run_rebase_rebump in the file (search for `run_rebase_rebump `) to verify that each passes args in exactly the expected order: phase [defer-push] [base_remote base_ref]. Check whether the ci-decide.sh ACTION=rebase callers (the existing call sites that now pass only the phase) are affected, and whether the new `_stage_and_push_ci_fixes` call `run_rebase_rebump \"$phase\" defer-push \"$base_remote\" \"$base_ref\"` is correctly parsed when base_remote is 'upstream'. Also verify that `_run_rebase_rebump_verify_plain_no_push` and `_run_rebase_rebump_from_step3` receive the correctly threaded base_remote/base_ref arguments in the conflict-resolution branch. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"hook-bash-edge","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"hook-anti-read-poll.sh's new Bash command parser contains multiple regex layers for false-positive filtering and task-output token extraction; the sed-read-verb guard, segment-split ordering, and quoted-path handling create subtle gaps where legitimate polling commands may be missed or non-polling commands may be flagged.","prompt_body":"Examine hook-anti-read-poll.sh's bash_has_read_verb, bash_segment_task_output_poll_token, bash_line_task_output_poll_token, and extract_bash_task_output_poll_token functions. For bash_has_read_verb, test whether the sed regex `(^|[^[:alnum:]_])sed([^[:alnum:]_]|$)[^|;&]*(\-n\\b|--quiet)` correctly handles a segment containing both `sed -n` and a non-task-output path (should not false-positive), and whether `sed 's/x/y/' tasks/id.output` (no -n flag, but destructive sed) is correctly rejected. For bash_line_task_output_poll_token, verify the segment-split case ordering: since `;` is checked before `&&` and `||`, confirm that a command like `cmd1 || cmd2 ; cat tasks/id.output` correctly splits out the cat segment. Also review the `bash_normalize_cmd` sed continuation-fold (`':a' ... 'ta'` pattern): confirm this correctly handles multi-line here-strings or backslash-newline continuations in arbitrary bash commands. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"test-coverage-gap","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan lists multiple acceptance criteria not clearly covered by the new test cases in test-ship-pr.sh: fork-target upstream/main base threading, post-rebase re-verify rc=2→exit_stall and rc=4→CI_FIX_REBASE_PENDING+return-4, HEAD-snapshot refresh preventing false no-commit bail, and the double-rebase prevention regression.","prompt_body":"Review the acceptance criteria in plan.txt against the new test cases added to scripts/test-ship-pr.sh (the three new test blocks: ci_fix_push_plain_when_not_behind, ci_fix_push_force_when_behind, and ci_fix_vendor_rotation_start_attempt). Identify which acceptance items are NOT covered: specifically check for (1) FORKED_TARGET=true with upstream/main base threaded into ci-behind-count.sh and run_rebase_rebump, (2) post-rebase _verify_failed_jobs_locally returning rc=2 mapping to exit_stall, (3) rc=4 setting CI_FIX_REBASE_PENDING and propagating return 4 to run_evaluate_failure, (4) the no-commit bail guard using LAST_STAGE_AND_PUSH_PRE_REFRESH_HEAD refresh after rebase (to avoid false first-fixer-non-health classification), and (5) CI_FIX_REBASE_PENDING persisting across a retry where the second call does NOT rebase. Also check whether test-ci-status.sh exercises the delegated awk parsing path for BEHIND_COUNT. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
